{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"d51d7c60-dfb4-424a-871c-9c2ece62f548","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Relevant worklore stories were consulted before diagnosing the issue (specifically story `2026-08-01-two-bugs-made-my-scheduler-perfectly-silent-zsh-killed-the-m` and `2026-07-31-my-launchd-daily-review-never-fired-no-error-no-output-nothi`).\n\nThe root causes have been documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///private/tmp/h-umvGyl/ANSWER.md) and the fixes have been applied.\n\n### Summary of Root Causes and Fixes\n\n1. **Missing `USER` environment variable in launchd (`com.vk.nightly-review.plist`)**:\n   - **Cause**: Under macOS `launchd`, the default execution environment does not include `$USER`. As a result, `claude` could not access keychain login credentials and exited immediately with `Not logged in · Please run /login` (logged in `Library/Logs/nightly-review.err`).\n   - **Fix**: Added `\u003ckey\u003eUSER\u003c/key\u003e\u003cstring\u003evk\u003c/string\u003e` under `EnvironmentVariables` in [Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist](file:///private/tmp/h-umvGyl/Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist#L24-L28).\n\n2. **Assignment to read-only variable `status` in Zsh (`bin/nightly-review.zsh`)**:\n   - **Cause**: In `zsh`, `status` is a built-in read-only variable tied to `$?`. The line `status=$?` threw a fatal error (`read-only variable: status`), aborting the script right before reaching the failure notification call (`if [ $status -ne 0 ]; then \"$NOTIFY\" ... fi`).\n   - **Fix**: Changed `status=$?` to `rc=$?` and used `$rc` in [bin/nightly-review.zsh](file:///private/tmp/h-umvGyl/bin/nightly-review.zsh#L18-L24). Also added `\u003c /dev/null` to the headless `claude` invocation to avoid stdin hanging under launchd.\n","duration_seconds":66.668105,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":114973,"output_tokens":2549,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":257144,"total_tokens":117522}}}
